# reda baked netlist -- generated, do not edit by hand.
# Regenerate with: cargo run --release --bin bake_verilog
#
# The netlist Yosys produced for the source named below, technology-mapped
# onto redstone_nor.genlib and read back by `reda::frontend`. It is checked
# in so a build that cannot run Yosys -- the browser viewer's wasm32 build
# above all -- can still load a synthesised circuit. A stale copy would
# misrepresent this project's own compiler, so
# `the_baked_netlists_match_fresh_synthesis` re-synthesizes and fails
# unless a fresh run renders byte-for-byte identically to this file.
#
# `gate nor y <- a b` is NOR(a, b) driving signal `y`. `gate merge y <- a b`
# is a wire merge (`Gate::is_merge`): no torch and no gate body at all, just
# the point where `a`'s and `b`'s dust are allowed to physically touch.
#
# 6 gates (1 wire merge), 4 inputs, 1 output.
circuit verilog:and4
source tests/fixtures/and4.v
top and4
input a
input b
input c
input d
gate nor g0 <- a
gate nor g1 <- b
gate nor g2 <- d
gate nor g3 <- c
gate merge g4 <- g2 g3
gate nor g5 <- g0 g1 g4
output g5
label y g5
